# Story 30: Instant Grids (##new grid) (50s)
# Hook: Spin up a whole grid of agent panes with a single command.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-030-instant-grids.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Spin up a whole grid of agent panes with a single command.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh. Building layouts by hand is fine, but the new grid command does it in one shot.

[00:08.0 --> 00:14.0]
Double-press Escape until the prompt shows hash-hash -- that's rysh mode for system commands.

[00:14.0 --> 00:24.0]
Give it a single number and it stacks that many panes into the current lane. New grid four builds a four-pane stack instantly.

[00:24.0 --> 00:36.0]
Add a dimension. Three by four lays out three lanes, each holding four panes -- a twelve-pane wall in one keystroke.

[00:36.0 --> 00:46.0]
Go further with three dimensions: tabs, then lanes, then panes. Two by three by four creates two tabs, each with three lanes of four panes.

[00:46.0 --> 00:50.0]
From one pane to a whole agent grid -- instantly.

